# `git.log`

Commit log up to `limit` entries.

**Policy** — read (C0, safe). Capability `ship.git.read`.

## Arguments

| name | type |
|------|------|
| `limit` | `number` |

## Returns

`GitLogResponse` (JSON).

| field | type |
|-------|------|
| `commits` | `map` |

## Invoke

```
ship ops call git.log --json '{ "limit": 0 }'
```

Kind: read.

## Example response

```json
{
  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "a1b2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c6d7e8f9012345678",
      "short_sha": "a1b2c3d",
      "author": "rust-lane",
      "date": "2026-05-24T18:30:00Z",
      "subject": "feat(checkout): scaffold the checkout service",
      "additions": 142,
      "deletions": 8
    },
    {
      "sha": "f4e5d6c7b8a90123456789abcdef0123456789ab",
      "short_sha": "f4e5d6c",
      "author": "code-reviewer",
      "date": "2026-05-24T16:05:00Z",
      "subject": "test(checkout): lock the happy-path contract",
      "additions": 67,
      "deletions": 0
    }
  ]
}
```
